      "text": "To solve the problem $3 \\oplus 1$ using the given operation $a \\oplus b = 3a + 4b$, we will substitute $a = 3$ and $b = 1$ into the expression.\n\nLet's break it down step-by-step:\n\n1. Define the operation $a \\oplus b = 3a + 4b$.\n2. Substitute $a = 3$ and $b = 1$ into the expression.\n3. Calculate the value of the expression.\n\nHere is the Python code to perform these steps:\n\n```python\ndef operation(a, b):\n    return 3 * a + 4 * b\n\n# Calculate 3 ⊕ 1\nresult = operation(3, 1)\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n13\n```\nThe value of $3 \\oplus 1$ is \\(\\boxed{13}\\).",
