      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve the problem \\(3 \\oplus 1\\) using the operation defined by \\(a \\oplus b = 3a + 4b\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the given operation**: The operation is defined as \\(a \\oplus b = 3a + 4b\\).\n\n2. **Substitute the given values**: Here, we need to find \\(3 \\oplus 1\\). So, we substitute \\(a = 3\\) and \\(b = 1\\) into the operation formula.\n\n3. **Perform the substitution**:\n   \\[\n   3 \\oplus 1 = 3(3) + 4(1)\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the individual multiplications**:\n   \\[\n   3(3) = 9\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   4(1) = 4\n   \\]\n\n5. **Add the results**:\n   \\[\n   9 + 4 = 13\n   \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(3 \\oplus 1\\) is \\(\\boxed{13}\\).",
